      "locked": false,
      "text": "Message DB\n\nNoSQL\n\n{\n  \"messageId\": \"m123\",\n  \"threadId\": \"t123\",\n  \"from\": \"a@gmail.com\",\n  \"to\": [\"b@gmail.com\"],\n  \"cc\": [],\n  \"bcc\": [],\n  \"subject\": \"Hello\",\n  \"body\": \"Full email body\",\n  \"attachmentIds\": [\"a1\"],\n  \"createdAt\": 1720748150\n}\n\nPK: messageId",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Message DB\n\nNoSQL\n\n{\n  \"messageId\": \"m123\",\n  \"threadId\": \"t123\",\n  \"from\": \"a@gmail.com\",\n  \"to\": [\"b@gmail.com\"],\n  \"cc\": [],\n  \"bcc\": [],\n  \"subject\": \"Hello\",\n  \"body\": \"Full email body\",\n  \"attachmentIds\": [\"a1\"],\n  \"createdAt\": 1720748150\n}\n\nPK: messageId",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WZEvAkhLuficF6zPcgGhR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4611.248748837843,
      "y": 41570.3519583616,
      "width": 1481.4069766532245,
      "height": 6165,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bELJG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 360968535,
      "version": 1590,
      "versionNonce": 396702828,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1777429058425,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "user svc:\n\nuser sends registration request and it saves user in user db sharded by email_id\n\nwhen user starts typing email in \"to\" field, system checks in redis cache and returns\nsuggestions (works for frequently used / recent emails)\n\nthis avoids hitting user db on every key press and keeps latency very low\n\nfor new email (which user never interacted with), no result from redis\nso once user presses enter or completes email → system fetches user details from user db\n\nafter that, this email can be added to redis for future autocomplete\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ncompose svc & signed url svc:\n\nuser opens compose box and starts writing email. \ncompose svc saves email content in draft db like to, cc, bcc, subject, body, attachment_ids\nemail is continuously saved in draft db so user does not lose data\n\nif user adds attachment, client first asks signed url svc for upload url. signed url svc returns\nsigned url. client uploads attachment directly to S3 using signed url\n\nso large file does not go through our backend\n\nonce file is uploaded to S3, S3 sends event to kafka\nscanner worker consumes file_uploaded event from kafka and scans attachment for virus /\nmalicious content\n\nscanner worker updates attachment db with status: PENDING / SAFE / UNSAFE\n\nif file is safe, attachment can be used in email\nif file is unsafe, notification svc notifies user\nand email should not be allowed to send with that attachment\n\ndraft db only stores attachment_id, not actual file\n\nactual file stays in S3\nmetadata + scan status stays in attachment db\nemail is continuously saved in draft db so user does not lose data\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nmail send svc:\n\nuser clicks send email\n\nmail send svc fetches full email content from draft db like to, cc, bcc, subject, body,\nattachment_ids\n\nit checks attachment db to ensure all attachments are SAFE\n\nif any attachment is UNSAFE → do not send email\n\nonce everything is valid, mail send svc moves email from draft db to mailbox db (outbox)\n\noutbox consumer reads new email via change data capture (CDC) or polling and pushes\nevent to kafka (topic: mail_inserted)\n\noutbox delivery orchestrator consumes this event and runs validations:\n    spam / malware filtering svc\n    policy check svc\n\nvalidation results are stored in validation db\n\nafter all validations pass → system checks receiver domain\n\nif receiver is gmail.com (same system)\n    → treat as internal email\n    → push to kafka (topic: inbound_send_request)\n    → delivery consumer consumes inbound_send_request\n    → stores email in receiver inbox (mailbox db)\n    → moves sender mail from outbox → sent\n    → notification svc notifies receiver that new email has arrived\n\nif receiver is external (yahoo / outlook etc)\n    → treat as outbound email\n    → push to kafka (topic: outbound_send_request)\n    → smtp relay worker consumes outbound_send_request\n    → sends email to external receiver SMTP server\n\nif outbound/internal delivery fails\n    → smtp relay worker or delivery consumer pushes it to retry queue\n    → after max retries it goes to DLQ\n\n\n\n\n\n\nsearch svc:\n\nwhen user searches email by subject/body/sender\nrequest goes to search svc\nsearch svc queries elasticsearch engine\nelasticsearch returns matching message_ids / email metadata\nthen search svc can fetch full email details from mailbox db/message db if needed\n\nFor indexing:\n\nwhenever new email is inserted/updated in mailbox db\nCDC / kafka event is generated\nsearch indexer consumes event\nand updates elasticsearch\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ninbound smtp svc:\n\nexternal email (from yahoo / outlook etc) comes to our system via SMTP\n\ninbound smtp svc receives and parses the email (to, from, subject, body, attachments)\n\nthen it pushes email to kafka (topic: inbound_send_request)\n\nfrom here it follows the same delivery flow (malware/virus/malicious file validations first,\nthen send)\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "user svc:\n\nuser sends registration request and it saves user in user db sharded by email_id\n\nwhen user starts typing email in \"to\" field, system checks in redis cache and returns suggestions (works for frequently used / recent emails)\n\nthis avoids hitting user db on every key press and keeps latency very low\n\nfor new email (which user never interacted with), no result from redis\nso once user presses enter or completes email → system fetches user details from user db\n\nafter that, this email can be added to redis for future autocomplete\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ncompose svc & signed url svc:\n\nuser opens compose box and starts writing email. \ncompose svc saves email content in draft db like to, cc, bcc, subject, body, attachment_ids\nemail is continuously saved in draft db so user does not lose data\n\nif user adds attachment, client first asks signed url svc for upload url. signed url svc returns signed url. client uploads attachment directly to S3 using signed url\n\nso large file does not go through our backend\n\nonce file is uploaded to S3, S3 sends event to kafka\nscanner worker consumes file_uploaded event from kafka and scans attachment for virus / malicious content\n\nscanner worker updates attachment db with status: PENDING / SAFE / UNSAFE\n\nif file is safe, attachment can be used in email\nif file is unsafe, notification svc notifies user\nand email should not be allowed to send with that attachment\n\ndraft db only stores attachment_id, not actual file\n\nactual file stays in S3\nmetadata + scan status stays in attachment db\nemail is continuously saved in draft db so user does not lose data\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nmail send svc:\n\nuser clicks send email\n\nmail send svc fetches full email content from draft db like to, cc, bcc, subject, body, attachment_ids\n\nit checks attachment db to ensure all attachments are SAFE\n\nif any attachment is UNSAFE → do not send email\n\nonce everything is valid, mail send svc moves email from draft db to mailbox db (outbox)\n\noutbox consumer reads new email via change data capture (CDC) or polling and pushes event to kafka (topic: mail_inserted)\n\noutbox delivery orchestrator consumes this event and runs validations:\n    spam / malware filtering svc\n    policy check svc\n\nvalidation results are stored in validation db\n\nafter all validations pass → system checks receiver domain\n\nif receiver is gmail.com (same system)\n    → treat as internal email\n    → push to kafka (topic: inbound_send_request)\n    → delivery consumer consumes inbound_send_request\n    → stores email in receiver inbox (mailbox db)\n    → moves sender mail from outbox → sent\n    → notification svc notifies receiver that new email has arrived\n\nif receiver is external (yahoo / outlook etc)\n    → treat as outbound email\n    → push to kafka (topic: outbound_send_request)\n    → smtp relay worker consumes outbound_send_request\n    → sends email to external receiver SMTP server\n\nif outbound/internal delivery fails\n    → smtp relay worker or delivery consumer pushes it to retry queue\n    → after max retries it goes to DLQ\n\n\n\n\n\n\nsearch svc:\n\nwhen user searches email by subject/body/sender\nrequest goes to search svc\nsearch svc queries elasticsearch engine\nelasticsearch returns matching message_ids / email metadata\nthen search svc can fetch full email details from mailbox db/message db if needed\n\nFor indexing:\n\nwhenever new email is inserted/updated in mailbox db\nCDC / kafka event is generated\nsearch indexer consumes event\nand updates elasticsearch\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ninbound smtp svc:\n\nexternal email (from yahoo / outlook etc) comes to our system via SMTP\n\ninbound smtp svc receives and parses the email (to, from, subject, body, attachments)\n\nthen it pushes email to kafka (topic: inbound_send_request)\n\nfrom here it follows the same delivery flow (malware/virus/malicious file validations first, then send)\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
